<speak>
  Let's look at a circulant Hadamard matrix.
  Its entries are plus one or minus one.
  Multiply matching entries in these two rows, then add.
  <break time="800ms"/>
  The sum is zero. Distinct rows are orthogonal.
  Each row is a cyclic shift of the previous one.
  H times H transpose equals four times the identity matrix.
  So we can study the whole matrix through the cyclic correlations of one row.
</speak>
